<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
<title>
  {%- if request.page_type == 'password' -%}
    {{- shop.name -}}
  {%- else -%}
    {{- page_title -}}
    {%- if current_tags %}{% assign meta_tags = current_tags | join: ', ' %} &ndash; {{ 'general.meta.tags' | t: tags: meta_tags }}{% endif -%}
    {%- if current_page != 1 %} &ndash; {{ 'general.meta.page' | t: page: current_page }}{% endif -%}
    {%- unless page_title contains shop.name %} &ndash; {{ shop.name }}{% endunless -%}
  {%- endif -%}
</title>

{%- if canonical_url != blank -%}
  <link rel="canonical" href="{{ canonical_url }}">
{%- endif -%}

{%- if settings.favicon != blank -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign image_type = settings.favicon | split: '?' | first | split: '.' | last | downcase
    if image_type == 'svg'
      assign image_type = 'svg+xml'
    endif
  -%}
  <link rel="icon" href="{{ settings.favicon | image_url: width: 48, height: 48 }}" type="image/{{ image_type }}">
  <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="{{ settings.favicon | image_url: width: 180, height: 180 }}">
{%- endif -%}

{%- if page_description -%}
  <meta name="description" content="{{ page_description | escape }}">
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Accessibility (WCAG 2.1 AA — 1.4.3 Contrast Minimum) safeguard, bi-weekly audit 2026-07-13.
  Three sitewide contrast failures measured on the live storefront (WCAG relative-luminance formula),
  confirmed against theme source. Independent of the open badge-contrast PR (also appends to this file) —
  trivial to resolve if both merge; no overlapping selectors.

    1. Top bar (announcement + inline country/language selector, .announcement-bar):
       near-white text #faf9f6 on the merchant slate fill #6a8b95 -> 3.47:1. Reuses the theme's own
       pre-darkened token --lll-slate-deep (#4F676E, already labelled "...shipping bar" in
       design-system.css but never wired up here) -> 5.7:1.
    2. Was-price / secondary text (--lll-text-muted, design-system.css): #848484 on cream -> 3.55:1,
       present on every product card (20+ instances per page on collection/search/home). On cards
       (.product-price--block .price__was) an additional opacity:0.5 compounds this so no text colour
       could reach AA there, so opacity is neutralised in that scope too. New colour #6e6e6e -> 4.84:1
       at full opacity (still visually distinct/muted from body copy, which is #5c5c5c).
    3. "Sale" nav link (--main-nav-link-featured-col, doc-head-styles.liquid): merchant setting
       nav_featured_col (#db3f30) on cream -> 4.19:1. Reuses the theme's existing pre-darkened
       --lll-sale token (#D03528, already used for the sale badge) -> 4.72:1.

  All three ratios verified programmatically with the WCAG relative-luminance formula against the
  live rendered colours on louloulollipop.com and louloulollipop.ca (identical theme + settings).
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
  :root {
    --lll-text-muted: #6e6e6e !important;
    --main-nav-link-featured-col: #D03528 !important;
  }
  .announcement-bar {
    --text-color: 79, 103, 110 !important;
    --heading-color: 79, 103, 110 !important;
    --link-color: 79, 103, 110 !important;
  }
  .product-price--block .price__was {
    opacity: 1 !important;
  }
</style>
